WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.770
So, listen, I don't pretend to know what's
going to happen in November with a presidential

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.770
election.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.750
Donald Trump may well get himself reelected.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.610
We did a story today about how Trump might
try to use a vaccine October surprise to get

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.840
himself reelected.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.340
Anything could happen.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.180
And all of the polling could reverse by November.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.710
But we continue to see polling signals that
four and a half months out from the election,

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.080
we can't ignore them.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.670
And many of them are state polls.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.490
The national polls are interesting to look
at.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.570
And we looked at that earlier when we look
at a place like Arkansas.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.730
The latest poll out of very red Arkansas is
stunning.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.930
Donald Trump is leading Joe Biden in Arkansas.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.859
Why only two?

00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:43.489
Forty seven to forty five.

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:45.670
Now understand that in 2016.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.039
Donald Trump won Arkansas by twenty

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:49.469
seven.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:52.460
Trump won by 27 in 2016.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:59.190
In 2012, Mitt Romney beat Barack Obama in
Arkansas by 24.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:05.740
In 2008, John McCain defeated Barack Obama
by 20 in Arkansas.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.850
Even if the five percent who are currently
supporting a third party candidate and the

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.030
three percent who are currently unsure.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.299
All go to Trump.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:21.159
Between now and November in Arkansas, Trump
would win Arkansas by only 10.

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.950
This would be the smallest margin of victory
for a Republican in Arkansas.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.790
I don't even know for how long.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:32.090
And it would signal some insane possibilities
for November.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.689
Also important in looking at the internals
of this Arkansas poll are that more people

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:40.579
disapprove of Trump than the number that approve.

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:42.719
This is a very red state.

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:48.340
So to see the approval numbers turn against
Trump in Arkansas is not a good sign for him.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.799
Senator Tom Cotton, a Republican whack job

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.649
from Arkansas, also is under water.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:56.759
He has disapproval of 47, approval of 44.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:58.579
So he's minus three there.

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:01.969
And where this is coming from is independents
in Arkansas.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:04.610
Arkansas has more Republicans than Democrats.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:08.340
As you probably imagine, the Democrats are
mostly not voting for Trump.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.470
The Republicans mostly are voting for Trump
right now.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:16.910
Independents in Arkansas are leaning towards
Joe Biden by six points.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:23.640
And so that may well be the group, so to speak,
that is going to cause Trump some trouble.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.280
Now, do I think Trump's going to lose Arkansas?

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.820
No, I don't think he's going to lose Arkansas.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.360
Is it likely that if the numbers stay this
tight, Trump will have to spend some money

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.360
in Arkansas?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.700
Yeah, it does become likely.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:42.460
And that's already a victory because any dollar
Trump has to spend in Arkansas is a dollar.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.540
He may not be spending

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.150
somewhere else.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:51.620
And if it is even remotely this close, it
is going to be a real problem for Donald Trump.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:58.630
And this is why, remember, every single one
of us has to operate as if Trump could win

00:02:58.630 --> 00:02:59.820
any state.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:03.470
Trump seemingly could lose some traditionally
Republican states.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:09.360
But we also have to understand that we all
must vote every single one of us.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.350
He won't be competitive in California.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.920
He won't be competitive in Massachusetts.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.460
But why take a chance?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:20.310
Why take a chance when the risk is four more
years, four more years of Trump, four more

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.100
years of environmental destruction, four more
years of being the laughingstock of the world,

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.760
four more years of Supreme Court choices and
all of the things that we have been warning

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:29.760
about.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.640
So very bad numbers for Trump.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.650
They won't change my behavior when it comes
to voting.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:36.650
And they

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:36.780
shouldn't change yours either.

